{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Error Correction When Transmitting Data ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about error correction when transmitting data.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Understand information about data and its structure in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Infinitives of Purpose with Present Continuous to Talk about the Purpose of Plans", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We use the <b>infinitive of purpose</b> to express the reason why someone or something performs an activity.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As you probably know by now, we use the <b>present continuous</b> form to describe those activities that we are performing at the moment of speaking (ongoing actions) or to describe any action that is taking place.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">However, if you want to express the reason why something is happening in either an ongoing action or a general action, you must use the infinitive of purpose.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The infinitive of purpose joins two ideas into one sentence, in which the first idea develops an action, and the second idea explains the reason of the first one to happen.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In order to make a sentence using the <b>present continuous</b> form and <b>the infinitive of purpose</b>, you have to use the following rule:</p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Idea 1\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Idea 2\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p><b>Subject + to be + verb ing + complement</b></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\"><b>To + verb base form + complement</b></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\"><i>Jane <b>is analyzing</b> the error solution software</i></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: justify;\\\"><b><i>to provide</i></b><i> precise tools to handle errors.</i></p>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Examples:</p> <ul> <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i>The company <b>is implementing</b> different schemas <b>to analyze</b> the possible errors in the program.</i></li> <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i>Jane <b>is talking</b> to the IT manager <b>to find</b> a prompt solution to the error handling problem they have.</i></li> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When we transmit data, errors are present in different ways during the process. For example, when the program is loading information from the web to store it in the cache of the computer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That's why engineers in the company are developing techniques to ensure the correct transmission of data.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Our programmers are implementing the checksum schema to correct errors.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Countable and Uncountable Nouns", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is important to differentiate what <b>countable</b> and <b>uncountable</b> <b>nouns</b> are.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When we talk about nouns, it is important to make the difference between&nbsp;<b><i>countable&nbsp;</i></b><i>and&nbsp;<b>uncountable&nbsp;</b>nouns.</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>COUNTABLE NOUNS</b></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Use&nbsp;<b><i>countable nouns</i></b>&nbsp;to make reference to those individuals such as people, things, and animals that you can&nbsp;count, that is, those nouns you can pluralize by adding -s or -es at the end of the word.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Examples:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pogram &ndash; program<b>s</b></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Disk &ndash; Disk<b>s</b></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Process &ndash; Process<b>es</b></p> <ul style=\"text-align: justify;\"> <li><i>The IT team is running some error correction&nbsp;<b>programs</b>&nbsp;int the&nbsp;<b>system</b>&nbsp;to ensure the quality of the&nbsp;<b>service.</b></i></li> <li><i>There are some&nbsp;<b>processes</b>&nbsp;we need to follow in order guarantee the&nbsp;<b>program</b>.</i></li> </ul> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>UNCOUNTABLE NOUNS</b></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Use uncountable nouns to refer to those things that one can perceive as a whole or a mass rather than an individual.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is important to remember&nbsp;that&nbsp;<b><i>uncountable nouns</i></b>&nbsp;do not have plural form; therefore, you always use them in their singular form.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Examples:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Software<br />Hardware<br />Information<br />Data*</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Note that the word&nbsp;<b><i>data&nbsp;</i></b>&nbsp;is the plural form of&nbsp;<b><i>datum,</i></b><i>&nbsp;but people commonly use data with either singular or plural verbs (data&nbsp;<b>is /&nbsp;</b>data&nbsp;<b>are</b>).</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Examples:</p> <ul style=\"text-align: justify;\"> <li><i>There is some&nbsp;<b>data</b>&nbsp;missing in the&nbsp;<b>software.</b></i></li> <li><i>This is a piece of&nbsp;<b>software</b>&nbsp;you can use to verify the&nbsp;<b>data</b>&nbsp;in the system.</i></li> </ul> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Remember that nouns can work as either the subject or object of a sentence. Therefore, you can use countable and uncountable nouns as the object or subject of the ideas you create.<i><br /> <br /> </i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Examples:</p> <ul style=\"text-align: justify;\"> <li><b><i>Error discovery software</i></b><i>is important for our company, that's why we use this&nbsp;<b>software</b>.</i></li> <li><b><i>Programs</i></b><i>are important for our company, that&rsquo;s why we use this piece of&nbsp;</i></li> </ul> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Notice how the words in bold work as the subject and object of the sentences.</p> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember that when we transmit data, errors are present in different ways during the process.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The simple coding of the program allows some wrong characters, but there are cases in which a large number of wrong characters become a problem for the program. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "transmit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to communicate or to transfer information", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are right; remember that when we transmit data, errors are present in different ways during the process.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "flip", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move quickly ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If there is a voltage drop, the electrical noise in the line can cause spurious bits or a bit flipping in the data stream. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "block", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of data together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It adds the binary value of each block of data, and sends them along with the block of information.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "reliability", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the degree in which something is trusted because it works well.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do not forget we can also implement the Hamming Code to provide high reliability, as it also corrects errors automatically. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "encrypt", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to convert or decode", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This scheme encrypts data and bits together to generate a code word in the file to ensure that the file at its destination only opens with the same code word.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look for more information about error correction in transmitting data.", "type": "text"}, {